# Lodestone - line ending normalization
#
# Why: the authoring machine has core.autocrlf=true and this repository had no
# .gitattributes. Measured 2026-08-24: 14 of 38 tracked files sat in CRLF in the
# working copy, among them plugin.cpp, PCH.h, Lodestone.psc and vcpkg.json.
#
# This file normalizes nothing that is already committed: the index is LF
# throughout, so "git status" stays clean after adding it. What it fixes is what
# lands in a working copy - here, and in every clone a consumer makes.
#
# Nothing here reaches into extern/: a superproject's .gitattributes does not
# apply inside a submodule.

# LF text - docs, C++ sources, build configuration
*.md              text eol=lf
*.txt             text eol=lf
*.json            text eol=lf
*.ini             text eol=lf
*.h               text eol=lf
*.cpp             text eol=lf
*.html            text eol=lf
*.in              text eol=lf
LICENSE           text eol=lf
LICENSE-MIT       text eol=lf
.gitignore        text eol=lf
.gitattributes    text eol=lf
.gitmodules       text eol=lf

# CRLF text - a tool requirement, not a preference. The Papyrus compiler reads
# .psc; cmd.exe reads .bat.
*.psc             text eol=crlf
*.bat             text eol=crlf

# No binary block here on purpose: this repository tracks zero binary files.
# Git detects binary content by NUL bytes on its own, and a public config that
# lists .bsa/.nif/.hkx would describe a project this is not.
